course: dictionary
lesson: 13707
title: Words for people who check things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a job, and the words around them tell you what that job is. «The inspector checked the kitchen to make sure the food was safe to eat.» The clues are checked and safe, so an inspector looks carefully at things.
explain: An inspector is a person whose job is to check that things are done properly and safely. A school inspector visits to see how well children are taught, and a food inspector checks that shops and kitchens are clean.
explain: Inspector can also mean a police officer, and in detective stories «Inspector Patel» is usually the one who investigates the crime. Read the words around the word to find out which kind of inspector is meant.
fact: An inspector is a person whose job is to check that things are done properly and safely.
fact: «Inspector» can mean a school inspector, a food inspector or a ticket inspector on a train or bus.
fact: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, an inspector is a police officer ranked above a sergeant.
fact: In detective stories, the inspector is often the detective who investigates a crime.
fact: The words around the word, such as «ticket», «school» or «crime», tell you which kind of inspector is meant.
exercise: «The inspector checked the kitchen to make sure the food was safe to eat.» What does an inspector do? | Sells tickets at the station | Cooks the food for the customers | *Checks that things are done properly and safely | Plays music for the school
exercise: Where would you most likely meet a ticket inspector? | At the bottom of the sea | *On a train or bus | In a library | In a bakery making bread
exercise: «Inspector Patel looked closely at the muddy footprints.» What is the inspector most likely doing? | Driving a bus | *Investigating a crime | Teaching a maths lesson | Serving food in a café
test: «The inspector asked to see my ticket before I got off the train.» What is the inspector's job here? | Repairing the train engine | Selling newspapers at the station | Driving the train | *Checking tickets on trains and buses
test: «The school inspector said the classrooms must be made safe for pupils.» What is the inspector checking? | Whether the teachers have new cars | *Whether the school is safe and properly run | The weather outside | Whether the children can sing well
exam: In the sentence «The inspector wrote a report after the visit.», what does inspector most likely mean? | A new school subject | A bus driver who drives fast | A type of bird | *A person who checks things and reports on them
